Subject: [PATCH] Supplement snapshot admission and buffered stdin acceptance

Exercise the production mutation admission lock with a held backend Start. Add an isolated source/clone fixture whose guest reader remains held while a bounded stdin sentinel is accepted, certified by existing IOProxy receiver cursors, and included in the actual restored checkpoint cut.

The observation temporarily prepares guest output senders and explicitly resumes them before ordinary CheckpointVM. Source and clone must each consume the captured sentinel once with preserved shell identity, accept independent later input, and finish through real output EOF without a trailing replay.

Test-only descendant of accepted Step3 332da2a7. No production code, build inputs, dependencies, binaries or image contents changed. Local admission race50, runtime compile and scoped lint pass; the new VM fixture has not been executed.

